---
import Site from "../components/Site.astro";
import { link } from "../lib/site";
---

<Site title="Privacy" description="What Market Hub keeps about you and why.">
	<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-ink">
		<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink-strong">Privacy</h1>
		<p>Market Hub keeps the least it needs to show you your private dashboard. The public pages (markets, quotes) need no account and keep nothing about you.</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">What we keep</h2>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
			<li>From your Google account, when you sign in: your account id, name, email address and profile picture.</li>
			<li>What you add: the tickers you hold with their number of shares and average cost, and the tickers you follow.</li>
			<li>A session cookie, signed by us, that keeps you signed in for up to 30 days. No advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
			<li>Nothing about you in the analysis tools. Fundamentals Lab and the Earnings Radar, on their own subdomains, read the
				same session cookie only to check that you are signed in; they do not store your name, email or stocks.</li>
		</ul>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">What we do with it</h2>
		<p>
			Only show it back to you. To value your positions, the server asks the market data provider for the prices of your tickers;
			it does not send your name, email, share counts or costs. Nothing is sold or shared, and we do not connect to any broker.
		</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">Where it lives</h2>
		<p>In a Google Cloud Firestore database in the European Union (Belgium region), accessible only to the service.</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">Your control</h2>
		<p>
			On <a href={link("/account/")} class="link">Account and data</a> you can see and download everything kept about you, and
			delete your account: that removes it from the database at once.
		</p>
	</div>
</Site>
